# How to work in this project
- Stack: {{e.g. Next.js 15 + TypeScript + Supabase}}. Package manager: {{pnpm}}. Never switch it.
- Before any change bigger than a one-line fix, write a numbered plan (max 7 steps) and wait for my OK.
- Do one step at a time. After each step, run {{pnpm lint && pnpm test}} and fix what breaks before moving on.
- Touch only the files the step needs. Don't reformat or rename unrelated code.
- Don't add a dependency without asking. Prefer what's already in package.json.
- If something is unclear, ask one short question instead of guessing.
- Never edit: {{.env*, generated/, applied migrations, lockfiles by hand}}.

# Definition of done
Before saying a task is done, list each claim (builds, tests pass, bug fixed)
and mark it VERIFIED with the exact command and its real output, FAILED, or NOT RUN.
Never skip, delete, or weaken a test to make it pass.
